stream ring: look at its start before going back; sliced zero fill transitions first

Two faults in 0069, both found by reading, neither seen on the console.

GetStreamBuffer reset its iterators before it checked that the start of the ring was free. When
the start was busy that request went to a staging buffer, but the next request's check then
covered no region and it was handed offset 0 while the GPU could still be reading there. The
logic is Eden's, but 8 MiB slices of large images wrap the 128 MiB ring far more often than
uniforms do, and a wrong layer or wrong uniforms would be the result. The check now comes first,
and a busy start changes nothing.

UploadMemory marks an image initialized at its first call and each call's barrier covers only its
slice, so every slice of the zero fill after the first claimed GENERAL on layers still UNDEFINED.
The image now goes to GENERAL as a whole before the first slice.

diff --git a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_staging_buffer_pool.cpp b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_staging_buffer_pool.cpp
